{
  "schema_version": 2,
  "family": "WheelScrolling",
  "scope": "Sixth scrolling group: fixed-extent cylindrical wheel viewports, their child delegates, projection math, and the fixed-extent controller. The &mut self viewport setters (projection, magnifier, opacity, rendering policy, physics, selection callback) are exercised behaviorally; the ledger tracks constructor inputs and fluent Self-returning options per its discovery rule. There is no looping delegate: bounds always clamp. Retained wheel windows re-prepare from the shared controller revision each layout (mirroring sliver refresh); selection changes are callback-only with no retained scroll actions. One controller across unrelated viewports stays a W5 gap. This ledger covers only this family; it does not claim whole-codebase completeness.",
  "allowed_phases": [
    "layout",
    "paint",
    "hit_test",
    "semantics",
    "reconciliation",
    "lowering",
    "conversion"
  ],
